<title>USA: NAFTA good for US agriculture -- ag-sponsored study.</title>
<headline>NAFTA good for US agriculture -- ag-sponsored study.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. agriculture has benefited from the North American Free Trade Agreement (NAFTA), which has spurred farm trade, a study sponsored by a coalition of U.S. agricultural groups said Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;Overall, NAFTA has been a significant net gain for U.S. agriculture. U.S. agricultural trade with Canada and Mexico has increased, and the U.S. has generally had a positive trade balance with both countries,&quot; the report found.</p>
<p>Canada and Mexico are the second and third largest markets for U.S. farm goods after Japan. In 1996, the U.S. exported over $6.4 billion to Canada and $5.0 billion to Mexico.</p>
</text>
